title: Interdisciplinary Reasoning SBA, Part 2 - Reflect and Review the Literature
authors: Comm360 Assessment Module
~~~~

Task 4: Reflect -- Is This Interdisciplinary? [id=reflect_start]
--------------------------------------

Ty: This list cuts across a lot of different subjects. I'm looking forward to seeing what kind of research we'll find for each of them.

Lianne: Yes, and we'll move into the research phase shortly, but first I'd like us to discuss our approach. At Comm360, we typically use an interdisciplinary research process like the one developed by Repko and colleagues in 2019. In the past, it has allowed us to combine insights into a holistic solution.

Lianne: So we'll need to determine whether the problem of people experiencing housing insecurity is the kind of problem that is appropriate for interdisciplinary research.

::homeless_broad_model_display [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_a label="View Repko criteria"]

Peggy: Ah, yes, I think all of us are familiar with the Broad Model from Repko from Professor Ari's course.

Lianne: Then you should be able to see how well housing insecurity fits the model. Why don't you all take a moment and evaluate it against Repko's criteria?

::homeless_first_pass_on_criteria [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_a label="Evaluate problem fit"]

--- wait @hl_initial_repko_evaluation.value ---

Peggy: Based on the Broad Model, we need to look at the causes on the list and see if they map to different disciplines.

Ty: And we should identify the disciplines we think would give us the most useful insights into the problem and possible solutions.

Lacy: How about each of us selects all the disciplines that we think apply for each of the causes listed? Then we can sum up our responses to see if they align.

::homeless_causes_by_disciplines [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_a label="Map causes to disciplines"]

// HACK: Object.keys().length is instructor-unfriendly. TODO: Add isFilled() or .numberFilled field
--- wait Object.keys(@hl_discipline_mapping.value).length > 4 ---

Peggy: I summed up our responses, and this shows any category that got more than one vote. We didn't always agree on each discipline, but overall we all see how different disciplines might investigate the problem.

::homeless_causes_by_disciplines_answers [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_a label="View mapping results"]

Lacy: Our analysis supports what you were saying, Ty. These causes cut across a lot of subjects.

Ty: It seems like an interdisciplinary approach makes sense in this case.

Lianne: We all agree that taking an interdisciplinary approach will work to study a complex problem like housing insecurity.

Task 5: Review Literature -- Economics Study [id=literature_economics]
----------------------------------------------

Lianne: Let's dig in now and get more information about some of the causes. We should be able to locate studies from some of the disciplines we identified.

Ty: I'm already on it. I took a few key words from one of the causes and did a search. This study looks promising. Take a look.

::homeless_econ_study_text [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_b label="Read the economics study"]

Lacy: This does look promising. Which discipline — or maybe disciplines — are represented in this study?

Peggy: I think it's Economics. There are some clues and jargon in the summary.

::homeless_econ_disciplines [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_b label="Select disciplines"]

--- wait @hl_econ_disciplines.value ---

Lianne: How are the clues you picked representative of the disciplines you selected? Can you explain?

::homeless_econ_explanation [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_b label="Explain discipline clues"]

--- wait @hl_econ_classification_explanation.value ---

Lianne: As you all recall, when interdisciplinarians locate a disciplinary source, they identify the "insight" of that source — often a recommendation, main finding, or conclusion that reflects the perspective of the discipline. What do you think is the main insight of this source?

Lacy: It seems to say that homelessness is related to economic conditions — like jobs and how the labor market works.

Ty: It's more specific than that. It keeps focusing on entrepreneurial activity and labor market freedom — and that when there's more opportunity in the economy, homelessness tends to be lower.

::homeless_econ_insight_input [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_b label="Write insight sentence"]

--- wait @hl_econ_insight_sentence.value ---

Lianne: Good work. Here are the sentences we suggested. Which one should we go with?

::homeless_econ_insight_choice [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_b label="Choose best sentence"]

--- wait @hl_econ_insight_choice_input.value ---

Lianne: Why did you choose that one? Explain.

::homeless_econ_insight_explanation [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_b label="Explain your choice"]

--- wait @hl_econ_insight_explanation.value ---

Lianne: I agree. The insight of this source is that **economic systems that create more job opportunities and labor-market flexibility are associated with lower homelessness.**

Task 5: Review Literature -- Income Support Study [id=literature_income]
----------------

Lacy: I used the search term method and found another study on homelessness. This one focuses on income support policies and family homelessness. Take a look.

::homeless_income_study_md [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_c label="Read the income support study"]

Lianne: Which discipline(s) do you think seem most representative of this study? Highlight the clue words.

::homeless_econ_study_text [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_c label="Annotate clue words in the income support study"]

Lianne: Now select the disciplines your clue words support.

::homeless_income_disciplines [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_c label="Select disciplines"]

--- wait @hl_income_disciplines.value ---

Lianne: How are the clues you picked representative of the disciplines you selected? Can you explain?

::homeless_income_explanation [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_c label="Explain discipline clues"]

--- wait @hl_income_classification_explanation.value ---

Lianne: As we did with the economics study, let's identify the insight of this source.

::homeless_income_insight_input [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_c label="Write insight sentence"]

--- wait @hl_income_insight_sentence.value ---

Lianne: Here are the sentences you all suggested. Which one should we go with?

::homeless_income_insight_choice [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_c label="Choose best sentence"]

--- wait @hl_income_insight_choice_input.value ---

Lianne: Could you explain why you chose that sentence?

::homeless_income_insight_explanation [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_c label="Explain your choice"]

--- wait @hl_income_insight_explanation.value ---

Lianne: Agreed. The insight of this source is that **greater access to cash assistance through TANF is associated with lower rates of family homelessness, suggesting that income-support policy design influences housing stability.**

Task 5: Review Literature -- Mental Health Study [id=literature_mental_health]
---------------------

Lacy: I found another study. Let's check it out.

::homeless_mh_study_text [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_d label="Read the mental health study"]

Lianne: So which discipline do you think is most represented in this study?

