Lianne: What do you think is the disciplinary insight of this source?

Lacy: This study seems to argue that mental health disorders are extremely common among people experiencing homelessness.

Ty: It also suggests that homelessness responses should include mental health and substance use treatment services, not just housing support alone.

::homeless_mh_insight_input [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_d label="Write insight sentence"]

--- wait @hl_mh_insight_sentence.value ---

Lianne: Here are the sentences you all suggested. Which one should we go with?

::homeless_mh_insight_choice [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_d label="Choose best sentence"]

--- wait @hl_mh_insight_choice_input.value ---

Lianne: Why did you select that one? Explain.

::homeless_mh_insight_explanation [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_d label="Explain your choice"]

--- wait @hl_mh_insight_explanation.value ---

Lianne: Agreed. The insight of this source is that **mental health disorders are highly prevalent among people experiencing homelessness, so homelessness responses should integrate mental health and substance-use treatment with housing support.**

Conclusion to Part Two [id=part_two_conclusion]
--------------------

Lianne: Good work! This ends Part 2 of the SBA. We reflected on whether homelessness is an interdisciplinary problem and located sources from different disciplines that shed light on its causes.

::completion_homeless_2 [display=target:homeless_p2_sidebar_e label="Mark Your Work Complete"]

Lianne: Next time, we'll map these disciplinary insights against each other and develop a presentation to share our findings.

